{"id":"erik-of-pomerania","order":2222,"name":"Erik of Pomerania","region":"europe-west","region_label":"Western Europe","realm":"Monarch of Norway","era":"middle-ages","era_label":"Middle Ages","blurb":null,"reign_from":1389,"reign_to":1442,"year_from":1389,"year_to":1442,"wp":"Erik of Pomerania","source":"wikidata","civ_wiki":null,"sources":{"wikidata":"ok","wikipedia":"ok"},"qid":"Q161958","wikidata_url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q161958","wd_label":"Eric of Pomerania","wd_description":"King of Norway, Denmark, Sweden, Kalmar Union","birth_year":1381,"death_year":1459,"reign_wikidata":[1389,1442],"image":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Erik_I%2C_1382-1459%2C_hertig_av_Pommern_konung_av_Danmark_Norge_och_Sverige_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15058.tif?width=640","family_qid":"Q655723","predecessor_qid":null,"successor_qid":null,"father_qid":"Q677904","mother_qid":"Q4965774","children_qids":["Q9254868","Q75387584"],"birthplace_qid":"Q497138","deathplace_qid":"Q497138","position_qids":["Q1294765","Q18341329","Q1268572","Q116"],"family":"House of Griffins","predecessor":null,"successor":null,"predecessor_id":null,"successor_id":null,"father":"Wartislaw VII, Duke of Pomerania","father_id":null,"mother":"Maria of Mecklenburg-Schwerin","children":["Erik","child1 of Pomerania"],"birthplace":"Darłowo","birthplace_coord":[16.41056,54.42083],"deathplace":"Darłowo","deathplace_coord":[16.41056,54.42083],"positions":["Monarch of Norway","monarch of Denmark","Monarch of Sweden","monarch"],"extract":"Erik of Pomerania (c. 1381/1382 – 24 September 1459) ruled over the Kalmar Union from 1396 until 1439. He was initially co-ruler with his great-aunt Margaret I until her death in 1412. Erik is known as Erik III as King of Norway (1389–1442), Erik VII as King of Denmark (1396–1439) and has been called Erik XIII as King of Sweden (1396–1434, 1436–39). Erik was ultimately deposed from all three kingdoms of the union, but in 1449 he inherited one of the partitions of the Duchy of Pomerania and ruled it as duke until his death in 1459. His epithet of Pomerania was a pejorative intended to insinuate that he did not belong in Scandinavia.","wp_description":"King of Denmark, Norway and Sweden (1381/1382–1459)","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erik_of_Pomerania","image_lead":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/Erik_I%2C_1382-1459%2C_hertig_av_Pommern_konung_av_Danmark_Norge_och_Sverige_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15058.tif","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Erik_I%2C_1382-1459%2C_hertig_av_Pommern_konung_av_Danmark_Norge_och_Sverige_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15058.tif/lossy-page1-960px-Erik_I%2C_1382-1459%2C_hertig_av_Pommern_konung_av_Danmark_Norge_och_Sverige_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15058.tif.jpg","chat_ready":true,"display_from":1389,"display_to":1442}